BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sunnycoast-13ol8l6@dothings
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260917T180000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Brisbane:20260917T200000
SUMMARY:Rob McWilliams Band at The Jazz Sessions
DESCRIPTION:Rob McWilliams Band Professor Rob McWilliams has led an interes
 ting life. A musician and composer\, playing trumpet\, flugelhorn and pian
 o\, he has been part of the jazz scene for many years\, originally playing
  professionally in Melbourne with artists such as Wilbur Wilde and Paul Gr
 abowsky. His studies and high level of musicianship led him to the USA whe
 re he took up the post of Professor of Music at the University of Wisconsi
 n\, Oshkosh and ended up as Head of Music there for several years. As a te
 acher he has presented at major music conferences in Japan\, Hong Kong\, t
 he UK\, Singapore\, Europe\, China and Australia and is a published author
 . As a musician he has performed with many jazz greats including Nat Adder
 ley\, Vincent Herring\, Dee Dee Bridgewater\, Eddie Daniels\, Ed Shaughnes
 sy and Dale Barlow – a resume that is the envy of many an Australian jaz
 z musician! A talented musician\, composer and arranger\, Rob has had many
  opportunities over the years to create and perform his music to audiences
  all over the world. Now living back in Australia\, he works for Yamaha Mu
 sic conducting music workshops around Australia as well as teaching at the
  Jazz Music Institute in Brisbane\, conducting\, composing\, arranging mus
 ic and performing regularly around Australia either as a side man or with 
 his own jazz ensemble. Though he is a Professor with an incredible and imp
 ressive Curriculum Vitae\, he is a warm and down-to-earth performer with a
  genuine connection to the audience\, bringing the music alive. This maste
 rful musician in now bringing his music to the Sunshine Coast\, performing
  with his band at The Jazz Sessions at The Presynct on Thurs 17th Sep. Joi
 ned on this gig by a stellar line-up of local Brisbane & Sunshine Coast mu
 sicians\, they have come together to perform unique interpretations of jaz
 z standards and some of Rob’s original compositions. Be prepared for an 
 evening of sophistication\, smooth jazz and world-class musicianship. VENU
 E & EVENT DETAILS 📅 Thursday 17th September 📍The Presynct\, Upstairs
 - 15 Ann St\, Nambour ⏰ Doors 6:00pm | Event 6:30pm -9:00pm 🚗 Parking
  available behind the Venue 🎟 Tickets $25-$45 🩴 NO Thongs Permitted 
 🚱 NO Outside Drink bottles If you’re looking for a unique concert exp
 erience\, look no further than The Jazz Sessions at The Presynct. This hid
 den gem offers intimate shows for listeners in a beautifully curated venue
 . These are listening concerts where people can come together to enjoy liv
 e music in a true jazz club experience. We ask that talking is kept to a q
 uiet whisper as audience members are actively listening to and connecting 
 with the artists in a relaxed and comfortable setting. These concerts give
  guests the opportunity to experience exceptional musicianship in an intim
 ate setting.
LOCATION:The Presynct Venue & Bar\, Nambour
URL:https://tickets.oztix.com.au/outlet/event/e1223444-6003-4f28-ab1c-5484a
 7cf1519
END:VEVENT
